                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "symmetrical":</h3><p><b>Symmetrical</b> ribbon microphones produce identical frequency responses from the front and rear side of the ribbon transducer &#8212; differing only in phase. Contrast with &#8220;offset&#8221; ribbons, which produce a different response from the rear of the microphone. Symmetrical ribbons can be used in Blumlein recording or as the side channel in a mid-side stereo setup.</p>
